  "method": "Each reset was preceded by writing a mark into every address the write probe found accepts any value, so that a byte the reset leaves alone reads as the mark rather than as its default. Only bytes read back as holding the mark are counted.",
  "each_preceded_by": "GS Reset",
  "why_preceded": "So the three are comparable with each other rather than each being read against wherever the previous one left the unit. This same probe measured that reset as reproducing the power-on capture byte for byte, which is what makes it usable as a starting line.",
  "write_probe": "data/units/roland-sc8850-01/write-probe/documented-40-4x.json",
  "subjects": "resets",
  "left_unmarked": {
    "prefixes": [],
    "addresses": 0,
    "why": "A mark written to an address that holds nothing lands in whatever store that address is a window onto, so a block of them says what the reset did to that store, under names that keep none of it. Skipping them is not a gap in the coverage: the store itself is marked and read under its own name. Anything listed here was left unmarked and this run says nothing about it."
  },
  "order": [
    "GM1 System On",
    "GM2 System On",
    "GS Reset"
  ],
  "stopped": {
    "at": null,
    "why": "The canary is asked every so often while the marks go in, and a run whose unit stops answering ends there rather than carrying on. Every number after that point would be about a space the run stopped being able to break, and a subject would be credited with restoring bytes that were never marked -- scoring better the worse the failure was. Where this is null the unit answered throughout."
  },
